-- Seed the IAAI (Insurance Auto Auctions) branch list into "yards".
--
-- Source: the public https://www.iaai.com/branchlocations page (its embedded
-- `locationsListVM` JSON), fetched 2026-10-03: 201 US branches.
-- yardNumber = IAAI branchNumber (e.g. Atlanta East = 707), the same number in
-- IAAI's own URLs (/Locations/707, /SalesList/707~US/...).
--
-- slug = the branch name slugified, which is the location id SalvageBid uses
-- for that branch's active listings:
--   https://www.salvagebid.com/search/location-id-<slug>
-- (verified for listed and unlisted branches: houston, abilene, atlanta-east…).
--
-- Nothing here touches Copart: the yardId triggers and every lookup by
-- yardNumber filter on source = 'COPART', so an IAAI number that matches a
-- Copart one cannot cross over. physicalInspectionAvailable stays false.
--
-- Upsert by (source, yardNumber) and gap-fill only: values an admin already
-- set from the Yards UI are kept. A slug already taken by another yard is left
-- NULL instead of failing the migration on the unique index.

